APPROVED
By Stefan le Bo ster at12:34am, Sep21,2022
CITY CONTRACT#
AGREEMENT FOR THE PURCHASE, SALE AND EXCHANGE OF LANDS
This Agreement for the Purchase, Sale and Exchange of Lands (Agreement") is made
effective as of the date of execution ("Effective Date") of the last signing party below, and
entered into by and between the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, amunicipal corporation organized
under thelaws of the State of Wyoming, having its principal offices at 2101 O'Neil Avenue,
Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001(City”), and MarkE is ele, King Ranch Company, P,10333Happy
Jack Road, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82009,(“King Ranch,”“Mark Eisele,” or “Eisele”), and
sometimes individually referred to herein as“Party”and collectively as“Parties.
WHEREAS, the City owns the surface and subsurface estate to lands situated in theNE%
of Section 23, Township 13 North, Range 68West of the 6"h P.M., Laramie County, Wyoming
("Parcel A"), encompassing 20.84 acres, having an appraised value of Fifty-Seven Thousand
Dollars ($57,000.00), which parcel is particularly described in“Exhibit A -Legal Description
and survey of Parcels A and B,”attached to this Agreement and incorporated herein by this
reference.
WHEREAS, King Ranch owns a surface and subsurface estate to lands situated in the
SW% of Section 14, Township 13 North, Range 68 West of the 6h P.M., Laramie County,
Wyoming ("Parcel B"), encompassing 13.85 acres, 13.85 acres and having an appraised value of
Twenty-Seven Thousand Dollars ($27,000.00), which parcel is particularly described in “Exhibit
A - Legal Description and survey of Parcels A and B,” attached to this Agreement and
incorporated herein by this reference.
WHEREAS, the City desires to trade Parcel A to King Ranch for Parcel B.
WHEREAS, King Ranch wishes to trade Parcel B to the City for Parcel A.
NOW THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual benefits and obligations set forth in
this Agreement:
Purpose of Agreement.Subject to the terms and conditions set forth in
Paragraphs 2-15:
The City agrees to sell to King Ranch, and King Ranch agrees to purchase from
the City, Parcel A;
b.
The City shall convey Parcel A to King Ranch pursuant to Wyo. Stat.  15-1-
112(b)(i) (West 2021); and,
c.
King Ranch agrees to trade Parcel Bin exchange for ParcelA.
2.
Terms of the Agreement.
